 "response": "ANSWER: $1905K\n\n**Status:** I added this up by hand once and did not run a second independent check. The final figure is therefore error-prone, and recounting the effective updates would confirm it.\n\n**What counts:**\n- Only Finance Office budget messages change the budget. Messages from other teams are ignored.\n- The starting point is #0001, which sets the budget to $1810K. No later message withdraws it.\n- I traced each withdrawal chain to its end before applying anything. If a withdrawal is itself withdrawn, the update it targeted comes back.\n- Every update that is still in effect is applied once, in record order.\n\n**Examples of how the chains resolve:**\n- **#0002 (\u2212$138K) does not count.** #1545 withdraws #0504, which reinstates #0031. #0031 then voids #0018, which reinstates #0005. #0005 withdraws #0002.\n- **#0035 (+$593K) does count.** #0920 starts a back-and-forth chain through #0331, #0176, #0119, #0110, #0084, #0078 and #0069. It ends with #0069 voided, so #0035 is reinstated.\n- **#0899 is voided by #1600.** That reinstates #0747 (\u2212$67K).\n- **#0987 is reinstated by #1593 voiding #1396.** #0987 therefore withdraws #0260 (+$572K), so #0260 does not count.\n\nThe running total of all updates still in effect ends at **$1905K**.\n\nANSWER: $1905K",
